[{"type":"markdown","embeddableConfig":{"content":"### Direct-from-AWS advisories
Events pulled straight from the **AWS Health API** (`aws-observe-and-protect-ad5bcf:metrics-aws.awshealth-default`, collected via the CPS-linked Security project over cross-project search). This covers scheduled maintenance, account notifications, and open issues AWS itself has raised about your account/resources.

**Trusted Advisor is not yet wired up** — no `aws.trustedadvisor` (or equivalent) data stream is being collected in either linked project, so no Trusted Advisor panel is shown here. Add the AWS Trusted Advisor integration to a Fleet policy to populate this section further.","settings":{"open_links_in_new_tab":true}},"panelIndex":"48489f89-ec80-4441-9fc0-9b412bd13a16","gridData":{"y":0,"x":0,"w":48,"h":7,"i":"48489f89-ec80-4441-9fc0-9b412bd13a16","sectionId":"9a1dbfba-eec2-493b-8d72-9cb154e5d433"}},{"type":"markdown","embeddableConfig":{"title":"","content":"### How to explore a resource further
Use the filter controls pinned above (EC2 instance, S3 bucket, billing service) to scope panels on this page. Then:

| Resource kind | Where to dig deeper |
| --- | --- |
| **EC2 instance** | Filter by instance name; check CPU / status below, or Discover on `metrics-aws.ec2_metrics-*` / `logs-*` filtered to `cloud.instance.name`. |
| **S3 bucket** | Filter by bucket; size table below shows stored bytes. Cross-check CSPM findings (once populated) for misconfigurations. |
| **Billing service** | Top estimated charges by service — often only populated from **us-east-1** even when `aws_regions` lists more. Empty other regions are expected. |
| **Trusted Advisor / Health** | Same home-region pattern — panels stay valid when only one region in `aws_regions` has data. |

